00:03:09.670 --> 00:03:14.170
episode

00:03:09.670 --> 00:03:14.170
"The Watchword is

00:03:09.670 --> 00:03:14.170
 ''Au Revoir''

00:03:20.870 --> 00:03:21.600
Oscar!

00:03:24.050 --> 00:03:26.750
Lately, the number of nobles who
visit the court has dwindled...

00:03:26.750 --> 00:03:28.430
...and it's become rather lonely here.

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:32.490
We didn't have enough money to put on
a proper funeral for Louis Joseph,

00:03:32.490 --> 00:03:35.400
so we sold off our silverware
and gold candelabra.

00:03:38.060 --> 00:03:40.530
The French Guards have their
hands full right now, don't they?

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:42.860
You didn't have to come and thank me.

00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:47.970
No, I had expected to be stripped of my rank
for such a serious violation of military order,

00:03:47.970 --> 00:03:51.510
but thanks to Your Majesty's mercy,
no punishment was handed down.

00:03:51.510 --> 00:03:52.870
I greatly appreciate it.

00:03:52.870 --> 00:03:57.590
Of course, we've been friends for 20 years now.

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:05.450
These are woeful times. We're both
forced to endure unpleasant things.

00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:08.860
However, this commotion will end very soon.

00:04:08.860 --> 00:04:14.480
The royal army is now marching towards
Paris and Versailles from all over France.

00:04:14.970 --> 00:04:17.120
The Light Cavalry Regiment from southern France,

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:20.270
the Royal-Cravate Regiment that
was stationed in Charenton,

00:04:20.270 --> 00:04:23.910
and the Salis-Samade Regiment that
was stationed in Issy, to name a few.

00:04:24.510 --> 00:04:28.250
Once they all arrive, their numbers
should swell to over 100,000.

00:04:28.250 --> 00:04:31.370
I ordered it as the Queen of France.

00:04:32.020 --> 00:04:35.820
I've summoned them to dissolve the National Assembly
and to prepare for the uprising of the people.

00:04:36.590 --> 00:04:38.460
The Louis Dynasty will be everlasting!

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:40.300
It won't falter from such matters!

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:50.770
French Guards Barracks

00:04:56.670 --> 00:04:59.540
Commander, it's almost time to go on Paris patrol.

00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:03.050
I'll be right there.

00:05:03.050 --> 00:05:05.540
Make sure everyone is assembled
in the parade ground...

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:07.110
Oscar...!

00:05:07.760 --> 00:05:11.620
I seem to have caught a summer cold
and have a slight fever, as well.

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:14.880
Sorry, but tell Alain to take charge
of tonight's patrol for me.

00:05:15.260 --> 00:05:16.090
All right.

00:05:16.090 --> 00:05:17.380
Leave the rest to us.

00:05:25.340 --> 00:05:28.640
Just as I thought, a sickness of the lungs...

00:05:29.240 --> 00:05:32.100
<i>The French Guards will be dispatched
eventually, as well.</i>

00:05:32.710 --> 00:05:36.560
<i>If we must, the royal family is
prepared to battle the rioters.</i>

00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:40.270
<i>When that happens, Oscar,
I'll be counting on you.</i>

00:05:48.130 --> 00:05:52.930
<i>The royal army arrived in Paris in July,
one regiment after another.</i>

00:05:52.930 --> 00:05:56.570
<i>The Royal-Cravate Regiment
closed Place des Victoires,</i>

00:05:56.570 --> 00:06:00.330
<i>and prevented the people from
gathering in the square.</i>

00:06:02.540 --> 00:06:05.130
We're not here to have a confrontation!

00:06:05.480 --> 00:06:08.140
We're here to have a lawful debate
concerning France's future!

00:06:08.750 --> 00:06:11.350
You're also Frenchmen,
just as we are, are you not?!

00:06:11.350 --> 00:06:14.310
Take off your military uniforms and join us!

00:06:14.310 --> 00:06:17.380
Yeah! If you're not going to join us,
go back to where you were stationed!

00:06:19.490 --> 00:06:21.780
<i>Meanwhile, the Royal-Allemand Regiment...</i>

00:06:22.190 --> 00:06:25.240
<i>...sealed off the road that connects
Paris and Versailles.</i>

00:06:26.360 --> 00:06:31.690
<i>They engaged in a skirmish with demonstrators
demanding Louis XVI to abdicate the throne.</i>

00:06:33.940 --> 00:06:38.080
<i>The Salis-Samade Regiment
patrolled Paris independently,</i>

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:41.710
<i>cracking down on nightly gatherings
and imposing a strict curfew.</i>

00:06:42.650 --> 00:06:49.520
<i>The situation had quickly grown
hostile in July of 1789.</i>

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:55.790
<i>Soldiers armed with guns were stationed
all over the city, intimidating the people.</i>

00:06:56.770 --> 00:06:59.960
<i>Also, another serious problem had arisen.</i>

00:07:01.030 --> 00:07:04.690
<i>With over a 100,000 soldiers flooding into Paris,</i>

00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:10.700
<i>the overpopulation had caused a severe
food shortage in and around the city.</i>

00:07:11.610 --> 00:07:17.250
<i>Hatred and hunger wiped away
the people's smile completely.</i>

00:07:22.580 --> 00:07:24.460
Oscar commissioned a portrait?

00:07:24.460 --> 00:07:27.550
Yes, she invited the painter herself.

00:07:28.190 --> 00:07:30.260
Why the sudden change of heart?

00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:33.060
She's declined every modeling request until now.

00:07:33.060 --> 00:07:34.050
If only I knew.

00:07:34.050 --> 00:07:37.530
I once saw you 20 years ago.

00:07:38.150 --> 00:07:39.480
20 years ago?

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:43.940
Yes, on the day the Queen visited
Paris for the first time.

00:07:46.900 --> 00:07:52.580
Back then, Lady Antoinette was still
a young girl and very beautiful,

00:07:52.580 --> 00:07:57.220
but what I remember most is your dignity and
innocence, as you rode right beside her.

00:07:57.220 --> 00:08:01.790
Your blonde hair shined like
the brilliant rays of the sun.

00:08:01.790 --> 00:08:05.630
You have been branded into this
old painter's eyes ever since.

00:08:06.830 --> 00:08:07.900
I remember, too.

00:08:07.900 --> 00:08:10.720
The sky was blue and very beautiful that day.

00:08:19.100 --> 00:08:20.270
Monsieur Robespierre!

00:08:22.850 --> 00:08:26.610
We've just been informed that Duke Orléans and his group...

00:08:26.610 --> 00:08:32.070
...are heading to Versailles, with 2000 demonstrators in tow and are demanding the abdication of Louis XVI.

00:08:32.420 --> 00:08:35.700
Make Louis XVI abdicate
the throne and then what?

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:38.160
They're advocating Duke Orléans'
ascension to the throne.

00:08:40.390 --> 00:08:43.000
Looks like Duke Orléans is finally
showing his true colors.

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:47.670
He joined the National Assembly and the Third
Estate representatives solely for that purpose.

00:08:48.300 --> 00:08:49.700
How ridiculous.

00:08:49.700 --> 00:08:53.800
If we accept that, it'll simply be a continuation
of the current rule by the aristocracy.

00:08:54.340 --> 00:08:58.140
Monsieur, let's remove Orléans and his
group from the National Assembly!

00:08:58.140 --> 00:09:00.080
Wait, wait. Just leave him.

00:09:00.080 --> 00:09:01.610
No one will support him anyway.

00:09:01.610 --> 00:09:03.850
Plus, we can't afford an internal feud right now.

00:09:03.850 --> 00:09:09.070
More imperative matters on hand are an official approval of the
 National Assembly, and withdrawal of the military from Paris.

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:10.690
Let us wait a little longer.

00:09:10.690 --> 00:09:14.960
Necker, the Finance Minister should
act on our behalf for our cause.

00:09:14.960 --> 00:09:16.030
Let us wait for that.

00:09:20.740 --> 00:09:21.830
Lord Necker!

00:09:21.830 --> 00:09:25.960
Do you realize you have spoken something a vassal
should never say in front of His Majesty?!

00:09:26.520 --> 00:09:28.210
I will offer my opinion again and again.

00:09:28.510 --> 00:09:31.180
It is no longer possible to ride
against the tide of the times.

00:09:31.180 --> 00:09:34.170
Instead of suppressing the National Assembly,
please approve it,

00:09:34.480 --> 00:09:36.810
and find a compromise through talks!

00:09:36.810 --> 00:09:40.980
Additionally, we must implement reforms
to overcome this current financial crisis!

00:09:42.250 --> 00:09:44.560
Just what kind of reforms are you suggesting?!

00:09:44.560 --> 00:09:46.020
Reforms to the monarchy!

00:09:46.020 --> 00:09:50.360
It is no longer possible for
His Majesty to rule France by himself!

00:09:50.360 --> 00:09:55.060
Without a parliamentary government that is founded on the cooperation from the new political power,

00:09:55.060 --> 00:09:56.950
a prosperous France will be impossible to attain!

00:09:57.300 --> 00:10:01.270
This new government and political power
you speak of are merely commoners!

00:10:01.270 --> 00:10:04.840
Are you suggesting His Majesty should rule
shoulder-to-shoulder with the commoners?!

00:10:04.840 --> 00:10:06.380
That is exactly my suggestion!

00:10:06.380 --> 00:10:12.150
Do any one of us here, who councils His Majesty,
have the power to resolve this crisis?!

00:10:12.150 --> 00:10:14.620
If you do, please stand up!

00:10:16.320 --> 00:10:17.880
Absolutely not, Your Majesty!

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:19.120
Absolutely not!

00:10:19.120 --> 00:10:20.890
You mustn't allow reforms to the monarchy!

00:10:21.330 --> 00:10:26.840
You proclaimed all resolutions that do not have
the King's approval are deemed invalid!

00:10:26.840 --> 00:10:30.900
If you approve the National Assembly now, imagine what would happen to the royal family's authority!

00:10:30.900 --> 00:10:32.910
The King's authority will be tarnished!

00:10:33.840 --> 00:10:35.190
<i>You mustn't give in!</i>

00:10:35.190 --> 00:10:38.910
<i>It is the King who creates the tide of the times!</i>

00:10:41.980 --> 00:10:44.330
You look rather pale.

00:10:44.330 --> 00:10:46.950
Let's cut today's session short.

00:10:46.950 --> 00:10:48.150
No, I'm all right.

00:10:48.150 --> 00:10:50.810
No, I'm also a bit tired myself.

00:10:51.350 --> 00:10:52.790
I see. If you say so then.

00:10:56.260 --> 00:10:58.790
Her illness seems quite progressed.

00:10:58.790 --> 00:11:00.890
I must finish it soon.

00:11:20.380 --> 00:11:22.950
Well, André? How was Paris?

00:11:23.500 --> 00:11:25.350
Freedom has disappeared.

00:11:30.860 --> 00:11:31.590
Oscar.

00:11:32.730 --> 00:11:33.990
What are you hiding?

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:35.630
Nothing at all.

00:11:36.060 --> 00:11:39.100
I may be blind in one eye, but I
can see everything about you.

00:11:39.100 --> 00:11:40.850
No, I want to see everything.

00:11:42.840 --> 00:11:44.300
Tell me.

00:11:48.380 --> 00:11:50.440
I'll go to Paris tomorrow, as well.

00:12:09.540 --> 00:12:12.290
Why are you being so hesitant, Monsieur?

00:12:13.020 --> 00:12:16.840
Just say, ''Do it, Saint-Just'' and I'll
head to Versailles straightaway.

00:12:17.260 --> 00:12:21.800
Louis XVI and Marie Antoinette... It won't
be easy, but it's not impossible.

00:12:22.840 --> 00:12:24.200
A demonstration by the people?

00:12:24.200 --> 00:12:25.500
Necker's persuasion?

00:12:25.500 --> 00:12:29.810
Monsieur, there are other things that are much
more effective, such as knives and guns.

00:12:29.810 --> 00:12:31.310
I have nothing to discuss with you.

00:12:31.310 --> 00:12:32.140
Now leave.

00:12:32.510 --> 00:12:33.640
How disappointing.

00:12:33.640 --> 00:12:36.340
Once again, you refuse to listen to my idea.

00:12:43.050 --> 00:12:44.150
Bernard.

00:12:44.150 --> 00:12:45.070
Yes.

00:12:45.390 --> 00:12:47.250
Keep an eye on Saint-Just.

00:12:47.250 --> 00:12:52.290
We can't have him ruin everything we've
worked so hard for up to this point.

00:12:52.690 --> 00:12:53.290
Yes.

00:12:53.290 --> 00:12:59.260
Go back! Go back! Go back! Go back! Go back! Go back! Go b—

00:13:01.550 --> 00:13:02.230
Go back! Go back! Go back! Go b—

00:13:02.230 --> 00:13:03.040
Go back! Go back! Go back! Go b—

00:13:03.040 --> 00:13:03.900
Go back! Go back! Go back! Go b—

00:13:03.900 --> 00:13:04.260
Go back! Go back! Go back! Go b—

00:13:30.530 --> 00:13:34.540
Commander, there's no point in
patrolling, even if that's our job.

00:13:35.270 --> 00:13:39.770
The Cravate and Allemand Regiments have
taken up positions along the street corners.

00:13:39.770 --> 00:13:42.460
All we're really going to be doing is taking a stroll.

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:44.160
What will happen?

00:13:44.160 --> 00:13:47.630
What will happen to Paris and
its people if this continues?

00:13:47.630 --> 00:13:48.970
Who knows.

00:13:48.970 --> 00:13:53.820
I guess wherever it'll lead is where it'll go,
unless the military withdraws from Paris.

00:13:53.820 --> 00:13:56.210
You mean... a riot?

00:13:56.210 --> 00:13:58.940
I'd rather you call it a revolution.

00:13:58.940 --> 00:14:00.150
A revolution...?!

00:14:01.610 --> 00:14:03.580
A revolution, huh...

00:14:05.950 --> 00:14:07.030
What's wrong, Oscar?

00:14:07.620 --> 00:14:10.990
I thought someone was watching us from in there.

00:14:11.360 --> 00:14:12.530
Want us to check?

00:14:12.530 --> 00:14:14.160
No, it's probably just my imagination.

00:14:28.220 --> 00:14:29.720
Stop!

00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:34.140
Vendôme Square up ahead has been sealed off!

00:14:34.140 --> 00:14:35.150
Take another route!

00:14:35.640 --> 00:14:38.420
We're currently on duty and patrolling Paris.

00:14:38.420 --> 00:14:39.350
Let us pass.

00:14:39.650 --> 00:14:40.690
Turn back!

00:14:40.690 --> 00:14:42.700
The Royal Cravate Regiment
has the area sealed off!

00:14:42.700 --> 00:14:44.320
Patrolling it won't be necessary!

00:14:44.860 --> 00:14:47.230
Hey, hey. Enough already.

00:14:47.230 --> 00:14:49.200
Can't you see our uniforms?

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:51.280
We're comrades in the same French Army.

00:14:51.280 --> 00:14:53.870
We've been ordered to not let anyone through!

00:14:53.870 --> 00:14:54.660
Now turn back!

00:14:55.000 --> 00:14:56.120
<i>Why you...</i>

00:14:58.580 --> 00:15:01.540
You blockhead! What part don't you
understand about moving aside?!

00:15:01.540 --> 00:15:02.810
Don't Alain.

00:15:02.810 --> 00:15:04.510
We can just take a different a route.

00:15:05.410 --> 00:15:06.740
Really?

00:15:06.740 --> 00:15:09.210
Well then, if you say so, Commander.

00:15:12.550 --> 00:15:14.420
What's the matter? Got a stomachache?

00:15:16.960 --> 00:15:18.130
Remember this!

00:15:18.130 --> 00:15:20.060
Paris doesn't suit you guys!

00:15:20.060 --> 00:15:23.610
You country boys should go back to where you
were stationed and keep the sheep in check!

00:15:23.860 --> 00:15:24.800
What?!

00:15:24.800 --> 00:15:26.830
Damn bastard has guts...

00:15:26.830 --> 00:15:27.910
Get him!

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:31.130
Don't, Alain!

00:15:40.410 --> 00:15:42.080
Oww...

00:15:42.450 --> 00:15:43.620
Are you all right, Alain?

00:15:43.620 --> 00:15:45.950
It's just a scratch. It's nothing.

00:15:45.950 --> 00:15:47.850
It's been a while, so it sure felt great.

00:15:48.660 --> 00:15:49.320
Alain.

00:15:49.320 --> 00:15:49.900
Yes.

00:15:49.900 --> 00:15:51.720
Let's round everyone up and
go back to the barracks.

00:15:52.130 --> 00:15:55.040
Just as you said, patrolling is meaningless now.

00:15:55.540 --> 00:15:56.430
Commander.

00:15:57.530 --> 00:15:59.350
About what we were saying before...

00:15:59.350 --> 00:16:02.170
If it turns into a revolution, the people will win.

00:16:02.170 --> 00:16:03.310
Just as you saw,

00:16:03.310 --> 00:16:05.070
the military has no cohesion.

00:16:05.070 --> 00:16:08.280
They won't stand a chance against the people,
who have been battling hunger for so long.

00:16:16.180 --> 00:16:18.520
Who are you following, Bernard?

00:16:20.750 --> 00:16:22.710
It's not me, is it?

00:16:23.190 --> 00:16:26.670
After all, we're both Monsieur Robespierre's protégés.

00:16:27.230 --> 00:16:30.760
Secretly following your fellow
protégé is an awful thing to do.

00:16:30.760 --> 00:16:31.550
I don't like it.

00:16:33.700 --> 00:16:35.200
Listen, Saint-Just!

00:16:35.200 --> 00:16:37.540
The world will soon change and naturally, too.

00:16:37.540 --> 00:16:39.470
Just as the leaves fall in the autumn.

00:16:39.470 --> 00:16:41.170
Why can't you wait for that to happen?

00:16:41.940 --> 00:16:42.850
Then, let me ask you this.

00:16:42.850 --> 00:16:46.110
Do you know Robespierre's true objective?

00:16:46.110 --> 00:16:47.110
A revolution.

00:16:47.110 --> 00:16:49.850
To create an egalitarian state
and a sovereignty by the people.

00:16:49.850 --> 00:16:52.220
You romanticize things. You're too naïve.

00:16:52.220 --> 00:16:54.590
Robespierre's true objective is power.

00:16:54.590 --> 00:16:57.640
He advocates for the people,
so he can seat himself at the top.

00:16:57.640 --> 00:16:59.730
To Hell with his revolution
and his cause for the people!

00:16:59.730 --> 00:17:02.750
In the end, Robespierre isn't much
different from Duke Orléans.

00:17:03.160 --> 00:17:05.270
Don't you trust him?

00:17:05.270 --> 00:17:08.600
He may have taken a leadership role,

00:17:08.600 --> 00:17:11.680
but it isn't so he can obtain power for himself!

00:17:11.680 --> 00:17:13.340
Cut the charade.

00:17:13.340 --> 00:17:15.050
No human can ever be truly trusted!

00:17:15.780 --> 00:17:18.580
No matter how history changes
its course or how the era shifts,

00:17:18.580 --> 00:17:21.480
humans are born and they die at
one point or another regardless.

00:17:21.480 --> 00:17:25.520
So, they're only thinking about
themselves while they're alive.

00:17:25.520 --> 00:17:26.970
Don't you see?

00:17:26.970 --> 00:17:28.720
I just want to do as I please.

00:17:28.720 --> 00:17:30.360
And that's terrorism?

00:17:30.360 --> 00:17:31.060
That's right!

00:17:31.060 --> 00:17:35.120
I'm much more suited to do that, than
become a leader or give speeches.

00:17:36.460 --> 00:17:38.200
Just wait and see, Bernard.

00:17:38.200 --> 00:17:43.670
He talks about negotiations and assemblies,
but what he's really after,

00:17:43.670 --> 00:17:48.040
is an opportunity to justifiably
kill off the privileged class.

00:17:49.180 --> 00:17:54.510
In that sense, he's also a terrorist,
but on a much grander scale.

00:18:00.790 --> 00:18:02.430
Jacques Necker, Minister of Finance!

00:18:02.920 --> 00:18:06.960
Not only have you neglected your duty
as Director-General of Finance,

00:18:06.960 --> 00:18:10.330
you have also made remarks that
insults His Majesty's policies!

00:18:10.330 --> 00:18:12.320
Your actions can no longer be forgiven!

00:18:12.800 --> 00:18:16.280
Starting today, I hereby banish
you from Versailles!

00:18:23.840 --> 00:18:25.710
Jacques Necker was dismissed!

00:18:26.150 --> 00:18:28.370
They got rid of Finance Minister Necker!

00:18:28.720 --> 00:18:29.410
Hey!

00:18:40.550 --> 00:18:43.700
Gentlemen, tell this to the people!

00:18:43.700 --> 00:18:47.630
''The King has finally begun to
persecute the patriots of this country.''

00:18:47.630 --> 00:18:51.740
''Starting with Necker,
a massacre will soon begin.''

00:18:51.740 --> 00:18:54.310
And make sure to add this part.

00:18:54.310 --> 00:18:56.740
''Now is the time to take up arms and fight!''

00:18:56.740 --> 00:18:58.280
''The time has come to rise up!''

00:18:58.280 --> 00:19:01.320
Monsieur, Necker hasn't been killed.

00:19:01.320 --> 00:19:02.910
He's at his house under disciplinary confinement.

00:19:02.910 --> 00:19:05.040
Do as I say!

00:19:09.870 --> 00:19:11.190
Fellow citizens!

00:19:11.190 --> 00:19:15.140
The King has finally challenged us head on!

00:19:15.140 --> 00:19:17.480
The time has come to rise up!

00:19:17.130 --> 00:19:18.730
Take arms, everyone!

00:19:18.730 --> 00:19:21.310
We mustn't let ourselves be manipulated
by those in power anymore!

00:19:21.310 --> 00:19:24.810
The King's Army is ready to kill off
all the patriots even tonight!

00:19:24.810 --> 00:19:25.970
To arms!

00:19:25.980 --> 00:19:27.770
Show them our strength!

00:19:27.770 --> 00:19:29.810
Robespierre is giving a speech!

00:19:29.810 --> 00:19:32.240
He's speaking at Saint-Martin Street!

00:19:35.270 --> 00:19:37.380
I only have two arms!

00:19:37.900 --> 00:19:40.210
But my passion and courage for our country...

00:19:40.210 --> 00:19:42.990
...is burning so fiercely, it's enough to
burn down the Palace of Versailles!

00:19:42.990 --> 00:19:44.160
Fellow citizens!

00:19:44.160 --> 00:19:47.090
Let us link our arms and fight as one!

00:19:52.870 --> 00:19:54.470
<i>Just wait and see, Bernard.</i>

00:19:54.470 --> 00:19:57.930
<i>He talks about negotiations and assemblies,</i>

00:19:57.930 --> 00:20:03.470
<i>but what he's really after, is an opportunity
to justifiably kill off the privileged class.</i>

00:20:04.410 --> 00:20:08.430
<i>He advocates for the people, so he can seat himself at the top.</i>

00:20:13.050 --> 00:20:14.490
<i>You're wrong, Saint-Just.</i>

00:20:14.490 --> 00:20:17.790
<i>It doesn't matter what kind of man Robespierre is.</i>

00:20:18.520 --> 00:20:22.410
<i>What matters is whether or not the people
are willing to stand up for themselves!</i>

00:20:25.170 --> 00:20:27.160
To arms!

00:20:25.940 --> 00:20:27.160
To arms!

00:20:28.900 --> 00:20:32.100
If you don't have a gun, grab a sword or a club!

00:20:39.580 --> 00:20:40.830
I beg you,

00:20:40.830 --> 00:20:44.010
please order the military
to withdraw from Paris.

00:20:44.520 --> 00:20:49.010
The royal family should never engage
in the killing of its own people!

00:20:49.010 --> 00:20:53.740
Oscar, if that happens,
you will protect me, won't you?

00:20:54.260 --> 00:20:55.650
I am...

00:20:55.650 --> 00:20:58.690
No longer in the Royal Guards.

00:21:13.780 --> 00:21:15.700
Please withdraw the military...

00:21:15.700 --> 00:21:17.180
Your Majesty...

00:21:17.180 --> 00:21:21.480
The royal family should never
point a gun at its own people!

00:21:23.090 --> 00:21:24.670
I'm afraid...

00:21:24.670 --> 00:21:26.840
I can't do that... Oscar.

00:21:35.570 --> 00:21:36.650
Oscar!

00:21:39.210 --> 00:21:41.440
Why the tears? As though...

00:21:41.440 --> 00:21:43.630
We'll never see each other again...

00:21:50.370 --> 00:21:51.860
Au revoir...

00:21:53.070 --> 00:21:54.560
Au revoir...

00:21:56.040 --> 00:21:58.070
<i>"Au revoir..."</i>

00:21:58.070 --> 00:21:59.400
<i>See you again...</i>

00:22:00.010 --> 00:22:06.580
<i>However, both Antoinette and Oscar knew
full well that they would never meet again.</i>

00:22:07.350 --> 00:22:11.730
<i>In the end, their longstanding
friendship was unable to triumph...</i>

00:22:11.730 --> 00:22:14.790
<i>...over the obstacle of being
the Queen of a country.</i>

